        <h2 style="color: green;">Understanding Generic Font Families</h2>

        <p style="font-size: 1.2em; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

            Generic font families help browsers choose suitable fonts. Serif fonts

            have small decorative strokes, while sans-serif fonts do not. Monospace

            fonts use equal-width characters. Cursive fonts resemble handwriting,

            and fantasy fonts have decorative designs. A generic family at the end

            of a font list provides a fallback if earlier fonts are unavailable.

        </p>

        <h2 style="color: rgb(40, 90, 160);">Understanding Color on Web Pages</h2>

        <p style="font: italic 16px 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;">

            Colors can be specified by their names, such as red, by hexadecimal

            codes, such as #FF0000, or by RGB values, such as rgb(255, 0, 0).

            CSS also supports other color formats. These methods let web developers

            control the appearance of text, backgrounds, and other page elements.

        </p>

